    "locked": false,
    "maintainer_can_modify": true,
    "title": "cli: Parse -signetchallenge like bitcoind",
    "user": {
      "login": "ekzyis",
      "id": 27162016,
      "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjI3MTYyMDE2",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/27162016?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/ekzyis",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/ekzyis",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/ekzyis/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/ekzyis/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/ekzyis/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/ekzyis/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/ekzyis/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/ekzyis/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/ekzyis/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/ekzyis/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/ekzyis/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "`bitcoind` returns an useful error when invalid hex is passed to `-signetchallenge`:\r\n\r\n```\r\n$ bitcoind -signet -signetchallenge=z\r\nError: -signetchallenge must be hex, not 'z'\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe error returned by `bitcoin-cli` only indicates that the RPC cookie wasn't found. It doesn't hint at invalid hex:\r\n\r\n```\r\n$ bitcoin-cli -signet -signetchallenge=z getblockcount\r\nerror: Authorization failed: ...\r\nIs your -signetchallenge correct for custom signets?\r\n```\r\n\r\nTo have consistent validation of signet args in `bitcoind` and `bitcoin-cli`, we now parse `-signetchallenge` in a new `ReadSigNetChallengeArg()` function which is called in `ReadSigNetDir()` and `ReadSigNetArgs()`.\r\n\r\nAddresses https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/34566#discussion_r3668123074\r\n\r\nI didn't add a release note because I don't think this change of an error message warrants one.",
