        }
      ],
      "message": "cli: Parse -signetchallenge like bitcoind\n\nbitcoind returns an useful error when invalid hex is passed to\n-signetchallenge:\n\n```\n$ bitcoind -signet -signetchallenge=z\nError: -signetchallenge must be hex, not 'z'\n```\n\nThe error returned by bitcoin-cli only indicates that the RPC cookie\nwasn't found. It doesn't hint at invalid hex:\n\n```\n$ bitcoin-cli -signet -signetchallenge=z getblockcount\nerror: Authorization failed: ...\nIs your -signetchallenge correct for custom signets?\n```\n\nTo have consistent validation of signet args in bitcoind and\nbitcoin-cli, we now parse -signetchallenge in a new\nReadSigNetChallengeArg() function which is called in ReadSigNetDir() and\nReadSigNetArgs().",
      "committer": {
        "name": "ekzyis",
        "email": "ramdip.singhgill@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-10-29T18:35:42Z"
      },
