      "body": "I checked if we're using patterns like here which could be refactored with context managers, but there's only one similar case I've found at interface_bitcoin_cli.py:205 where we comment out `rpcport` in the config before running some tests and restoring it.\n\nIn the other cases, we're either restarting the node with the new changes (so undo is undesired) or `node.replace_in_config()` is more ergonomic.\n\nSo in case someone has more context than me to still consider this a good idea: This and similar patterns could be refactored with a context manager like this:\n\n```python\nwith extra_config(node, \"signetchallenge=51\"):\n    assert_raises_process_error(1, \"-signetchallenge cannot be multiple values.\", node.cli(\"-signetchallenge=51\").getblockcount)\n```",
